{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass when Moses came down.</b> When he brought the last tablets on the Day of Atonement." "<b>That the skin of his face sent forth beams.</b> קָרַן is a term of horns — the light flashed and projected like a kind of horn. And from where did Moses merit these horns of splendor? Our Rabbis said: from the cave, when the Holy One, blessed be He, placed His hand over his face, as it says ״וְשַׂכֹּתִי כַפִּי״ (Tanchuma)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:37.060296485Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}